# Your Anthropic API key. Without one, CourseForge runs its offline mock
# generator: courses come out structurally complete but the prose is
# placeholder, which is enough to exercise the studio, the player and every
# export, and not enough to teach anyone anything.
# Create a key at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Which model writes the courses. Defaults to claude-opus-5.
# COURSE_FORGE_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Optional. How hard the model works per request: low, medium, high, xhigh or
# max. Defaults to high. Lower it to cut cost on drafts; raise it for courses
# going to real learners.
# COURSE_FORGE_EFFORT=high

# Optional. Force a generator regardless of credentials: anthropic or mock.
# COURSE_FORGE_PROVIDER=

# Optional. Ceiling on the response length for a single lesson or quiz.
# Raise it if long lessons come back truncated.
# COURSE_FORGE_MAX_TOKENS=16000

# Optional. Set to 1 to pin every request to COURSE_FORGE_MODEL instead of
# letting the API reroute a request its safety classifiers decline.
# COURSE_FORGE_DISABLE_FALLBACKS=

# Optional. Where courses are stored. Defaults to ./data/courses.
# COURSE_FORGE_DATA_DIR=

# Optional. Port for the API and the built studio. Defaults to 5174.
# PORT=5174
